[0.11.0]
- Feature: "Income vs. spending" at the top of the dashboard, always visible and
  independent of the date picker — income and spending per calendar month for the
  last 12 months, with the monthly average of spending, income and what is left over.
  Spending is every withdrawal, income every deposit; transfers between own accounts
  are left out, so the salary (deposit into Paycheck, then transferred on) counts once.
  The running month is drawn faded and kept out of the averages
- Totals come from Firefly's insight endpoints (/insight/expense/total,
  /insight/income/total): 26 small requests instead of a year of transactions

[0.10.4]
- Fixed costs: renamed to "Fixed monthly spendings", on a highlighted background, with a
  one-line explanation of what the section is for — "Fixed costs" alone did not say that
  these are the commitments you cannot cancel on short notice. The highlight uses the tag
  palette, not amber, so it does not read as another "not booked" warning
- Fixed costs: the footer toggle said "Show all N items" without saying what the other
  items were. It now names them: "Show N recurring items not charged this month",
  and disappears when there are none
- Fixed costs: headline count reads "N charged so far" instead of "N items"
- Fixed costs: cadence and due date now come from the Firefly bill when a transaction
  carries one, instead of being inferred from past charges. An item that moved from the
  1st to the 20th no longer reads as overdue for three weeks, quarterly items say
  "quarterly" instead of "irregular", and rows show the bill's next expected date.
  Bills already loaded for the Bills section, so this costs no extra request.
  Inactive bills are ignored and fall back to the inferred cadence
- Fixed costs: items last charged over three months ago (and beyond twice their own
  charge interval) are flagged "possibly cancelled" — a dead tag otherwise sits in the
  list forever and drags the 12-month average
- Fixed costs: a month mixing currencies now says so. Amounts were being summed at face
  value with no conversion; that still happens, but it is no longer silent

[0.10.3]
- Fixed costs: sort by what an item costs when charged (this month's amount, or its
  expected amount if not booked yet), so a rent that has not hit yet stays at the top
  instead of sinking below a €14 subscription
- Fixed costs: dormant rows now say "not this month" instead of showing a bare dash

[0.10.2]
- Fix: fixed costs took minutes to load. Firefly's tag endpoint returns every match
  on page one but reports the *unfiltered* transaction count in meta.pagination
  ("24 pages" for 62 results), so pagination walked 23 empty pages at ~1.2s each.
  Paging now stops on the first short page — 24 requests down to 1
- Fixed costs: bigger total, and a real spinner while the 12 months load

[0.10.1]
- Fix: Docker build no longer upgrades npm inside the image. npm 12 requires
  Node ^22.22.2 while node:22-alpine ships 22.22.1, so `npm install -g npm@latest`
  broke every build the day npm 12 landed. The bundled npm builds the client fine,
  and the build no longer depends on what npm published today.

[0.10.0]
- Feature: "Fixed costs" report — every transaction tagged "monthly recurring expense",
  rolled up per month. Sits under the period summary, collapsed by default,
  open state kept in the URL (?fixed=1)
- Shows the month's total, item count, share of income, and the 12-month average
- Per-item table grouped by bill → payee → description, with the expected amount
  (6-month median), last charge date, and a flag when a charge drifts >5% from its median
- Flags recurring items not yet booked this month, once their usual due day has passed
- 12-month bar strip; click a bar to re-anchor the report to that month
- Transfers count toward fixed costs (a paycheck arrives as a transfer here, so
  transfers are real money movements); tagged deposits are ignored and flagged as
  likely tagging slips
- Tag matching is case-insensitive
- API: new firefly.taggedTransactions() using Firefly's tag endpoint, with a fallback
  to a full transaction scan if that endpoint is unavailable
- Fix: Firefly pagination is now followed to the last page instead of silently
  keeping only the first — long windows no longer understate totals
- Chore: split-flattening extracted to one helper; formatters moved to client/src/format.js

[0.9.1]
- Fix: include transfer in default filterTypes, fix URL sync accordingly

[0.9.0]
- Feature: filter state syncs bidirectionally with URL search params — dashboard
  views are now shareable and survive a reload

[0.8.7]
- update readme regarding token settings

[0.8.6]
- Revert: client-side error message formatting (caused raw JSON parse errors to surface)
- Note: if you see auth errors, recreate your Personal Access Token in Firefly-III
  (Profile → OAuth → Personal Access Tokens)

[0.8.5]
- Fix: proxy now detects when Firefly-III redirects to login (expired/invalid token)
  and returns a clear HTTP 401 instead of a confusing JSON parse error
- Fix: guard against non-JSON responses from misconfigured reverse proxies
- Fix: error messages now include the Node.js error code (e.g. ECONNREFUSED),
  the target URL, and the raw detail — making connection issues actionable
- Chore: remove unused SESSION_SECRET from .env.example
